WEBVTT

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.810
Interview Room

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.850
I don't know anything about programming.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.900
Should I really be an interviewer?

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.750
It won't be an issue. 
I know the applicant's skill level.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.460
Think of this as a personality assessment.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.290
Interview Room

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.290
Please, come in.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.080
Huh?

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.300
Pardon me!

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.010
Nenecchi?!

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.480
A-Aocchi?! Why are you here?

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:17.150
Excuse me, "Aocchi"? 
You are in an interview right now.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.240
Oh!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.330
Suzukaze-san...

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.870
Yes, that is correct.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.660
<i>Wh-What's going on here?</i>

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.250
<i>Are they messing with me?!</i>

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:35.590
Please introduce yourself.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.290
Oh, right.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.770
I'm Sakura Nene from 
Kirara Women's University.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.340
Please, have a seat.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.640
Thank you.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.900
I-Is something wrong?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.150
N-No. It's just, you're being 
so mindful of your manners.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.450
First, let's hear why you 
applied for this job.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.270
Do I really have to say that 
in front of Ao—Suzukaze-san?

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:12.460
Is your motivation something 
Suzukaze-san shouldn't hear?

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:17.710
No, but...

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:24.600
Um... When I worked part-time 
debugging at your company last year,

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:29.230
the atmosphere and approach to your 
projects left a deep impression on me,

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:35.020
and encouraged me to apply 
for a programming position here.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.890
Wow. I had no idea you'd 
been thinking about that.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:41.200
This is so awkward!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.630
<i>But does their doing this mean 
I'm already as good as hired?</i>

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.910
<i>No, hang on! This is 
Umiko-san we're talking about.</i>

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.050
<i>It's got to be some kind of trap!</i>

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.250
Nenecchi!

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.510
<i>When Aocchi's around, I...</i>

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.190
<i>I... let my guard down!</i>

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:56.940
I've gotcha!

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.510
<b>Game Over</b>

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:03.010
<i>That's right! The moment I take 
this lightly, it's all over!</i>

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.510
Suzukaze-san.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:11.370
Do you have any questions for Sakura-san?

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:16.360
Um... When did you first consider 
working for our company?

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.660
<i>A canned response won't work on them.</i>

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:25.730
T-To be honest, 
I simply found the debugging work fun,

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:29.540
so I was just hoping I could do it again.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:35.050
But... But then I heard you'd 
stopped hiring part-time debuggers,

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:39.180
so mostly on a whim, 
I started doing some programming.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.550
Doing so helped me understand 
the incredible devotion

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:48.360
that Ao—Suzukaze-san and her team 
put into making their games.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.740
The experience of creating my own game

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:55.100
naturally inspired me to 
want to work here again!

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.460
Thank you.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.760
Suzukaze-san, do you have anything else?

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.610
N-No, not right now.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:10.770
Well then, Suzukaze-san, thank you. 
You may take your leave.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.770
Wait, me?!

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.650
If you'll excuse me...

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.920
Nenecchi, do your best!

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.690
<i>Now the real interview begins!</i>

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.640
Congratulations.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.390
Huh?

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.310
You did well to stay on your toes.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.480
You pass, Sakura-san.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.480
Since you're still a student,

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.640
per your request, we'd like to offer you

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:47.930
a three-month part-time contract 
working three days a week to start with.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.240
Thank you so much!

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.240
However, I should warn 
you about a few things.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:06:01.130
You are not yet up to the skill level 
required of a programmer at our company.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:05.750
But in light of your enthusiasm 
and how fast you've learned,

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:09.130
I talked to the president and 
obtained approval to hire you.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:14.820
For the time being, you'll be given 
training assignments and odd jobs.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:19.370
It might be rough for you, 
given your current lack of skill.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.370
However...

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.570
Listen well, because I'm 
only going to say this once.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:30.360
I have high hopes for you 
right now, Sakura-san.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:42.340
For now, focus your efforts on getting 
your contract renewed in three months.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.930
No one's ever said they had 
high hopes for me before in my life!

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.050
I won't let you down!

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.320
Aocchi!

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.690
I passed!

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:56.970
Already?!

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.860
Huh? Nene-chan, you're joining the company?

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:00.560
Yes!

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:04.900
I'll be starting part-time, 
but I look forward to working with everyone!

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.840
Congratulations, Nenecchi!

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.620
Thanks, Aocchi.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.970
Ah, Aocchi, is that...

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:14.650
Huh?

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.120
You're really doing character design!

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.800
Can I have a look?

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.650
S-Sure...

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:24.080
So <i>PECO was</i> you!

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:29.340
The gaming magazine credited Yagami-san, 
so I thought I'd guessed wrong.

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:35.690
It was decided that Yagami-san would do 
the key visuals for the adverts,

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.980
whereas I'm the internal designer.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.850
That's amazing, Aocchi! 
You've moved up so much!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:43.890
Huh?

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:48.700
It's got your dark, surreal touch. 
Such a fun style!

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.770
What's the matter, Aocchi?

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.160
It's nothing.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.910
You couldn't have come 
at a better time, Nenecchi.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:11.270
Is it still bugging you? 
You're going to ruin your pretty face.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:17.870
If only I had more power, 
I could have fought the company's decision!

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:21.020
I'll make sure <i>PECO</i> sells, no matter what!

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.630
I'm counting on you.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:24.440
I'll make sure...

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.450
So tonight, I'm gonna drink the night away!

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.530
Okay, okay. I'll keep you company.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:31.780
But!

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.750
Thanks to that key visual,

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:37.970
offers are pouring in from magazines 
that want to cover the game!

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.670
It was a job well done!

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.210
It sure was.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:44.290
But it was a job handled in the worst way.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:48.390
After what happened, 
the character team must hate me.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:52.010
How am I supposed to ask 
them for promo art now?

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.050
I know a trick that'll get you 
on the character team's good side.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.410
Would you like to give it a try, meow?

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:12.730
Charm

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:11.340
I put all of my love in this,

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.970
so know you're in good hands and go get 'em!

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:19.120
And when you return triumphant,

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.500
I expect a passionate embrace...

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:24.190
Toyama-san, if you would adjust the schedule.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:25.620
Certainly...

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.460
Charm

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.470
Hey, stop that!

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.720
Mozuku-chan, I'm working right now, okay?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.980
Come on. I'll play with you later.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:50.040
Yagami-san, do you have a moment?

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.740
With the buzz after the reveal, 
numerous companies have sent us offers.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.240
Requests for <i>PECO</i> official art

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:03.620
I don't mind doing exclusive art, 
but isn't this a bit much?

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.220
My job is to make games.

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:11.200
As well as to promote them.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:16.310
They've allocated pages for us with 
the expectation of your exclusive art.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:21.310
I've made sure both the deadlines and 
compensation will be quite generous.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.600
H-Hang on a sec.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.690
I'm sorry.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:31.230
So, what do you say?

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:40.580
Fine. If they want art, they'll get it.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.230
This is gonna mess up my groove.

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:46.350
Thank you. That's a load off my mind.

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:52.130
<i>They really do hate me.</i>

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:54.890
If you'll excuse me.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:56.270
Oh, sure.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.370
What happened?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.420
Catnip?

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.310
Are you all right?

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:23.700
Oh, pardon me.

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:26.990
Thank you.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.130
No problem.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:44.550
P-Please, stay away!

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.790
I-I'm sorry...

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:50.830
Oh...

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:56.020
It's just, um...

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:03.910
I'm not comfortable with people touching 
or getting too close to me.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:11.540
I'm sorry.

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:16.110
Oh, I see.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.390
I'm sorry, I had no idea...

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:21.130
It's fine. I appreciate your understanding.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:31.220
Um, Yamato-san, your full name is 
Yamato Christina Wako-san, right?

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:33.830
Huh? Y-Yes, it is.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.900
I'm half-French, on my mother's side.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.490
Your mother's French?

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:41.730
Oh, my friend said that 
they greet people by kissing.

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:43.030
Right...

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:45.310
They do, indeed...

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:48.060
Sh-Should I not have mentioned that?

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:52.380
It's just, my family back in France, 
especially my younger sister,

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:56.250
are overly fond of greetings, 
so you can imagine....

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.740
I see.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.500
So you came to Japan by yourself?

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:05.010
Yes. My love of Japanese 
video games brought me here.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.810
My sister is also making games in France.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:09.600
What kind of games?

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:15.350
Well, they're working on a VR game 
about exploring ancient towns.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.100
Good sales

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.100
Welcome back. How'd it go?

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:21.430
Yagami-san accepted the promo art job.

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:24.030
Now, you know that's not what I meant.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.270
Are you on the character 
team's good side now?

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:28.350
Yes. You were a big help.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:29.950
Thank you, Mozuku.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:36.410
That's no fair, Mozuku! 
She's never even kissed me before!

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:39.000
And I never will.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.380
S-So I'm finally going to be a s-senpai?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.500
Congrats, Aoba-chan!

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.330
As if you're not equally 
worked up about it, Hajime.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:56.350
Wh-Wh-What if they're older?

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:59.050
You'll just have to wait and see.

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:00.560
'Course, I already know.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:04.390
Oh, but this cubicle 
is already fully occupied.

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:09.470
And seating the newbie next to me
 will just make them nervous.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:13.080
The best option would be 
to have someone here move.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:20.000
W-Wait a sec! As the sole motion team 
member here, I'd be the prime candidate!

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:24.150
It's gonna feel lonely, 
with the rambunctious one gone.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.260
So it's a done deal?!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.720
W-Would you really be 
okay with me leaving, Yun?

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:36.530
Huh? I-I wouldn't not be unbothered by it...

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:37.810
So which is it?

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.420
Why not put their seat 
in the middle of the cubicle?

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:43.110
What is that, hazing?

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.370
Let's just rock-paper-scissors.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:46.100
Um...

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.900
Yeah. That's most fair.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.900
U-Um...

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.780
Okay! Rock, paper...

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.030
Um!

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:56.020
Uh, u-um...

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:02.000
I can... go sit next to Ko-chan.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:07.470
Well, that's probably best. 
Hifumin is the team leader, after all.

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:12.220
Still, it'll be kinda lonely without you.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.710
No, it'll be okay.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.620
I'll come by every day... 
to check on your progress.

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:21.730
E-Er, you can come by without a reason!

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:23.920
<i>A new person, huh?</i>

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.790
<i>I can't wait to meet them!</i>

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.450
<b>SuFamitsu</b>

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.410
What's wrong, Momo?

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:37.820
<i>PECO</i>'s designs don't look 
like Yagami Ko-san's.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:39.160
Huh? How so?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.990
I mean, she's the one credited, right?

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:46.500
Yeah. But they just look...

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.510
kinda dumb?

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:54.180
Isn't it great that we both 
got to come here as interns?

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.010
Suzuran

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:54.950
Yeah.

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.470
E-Excuse me!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:02.190
Could you two be Eagle Jump's new hires?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.170
Yes, we are.

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:09.190
Oh, I knew it! My name is 
Suzukaze Aoba, and I work here!

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.580
N-Nice to meet you...

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:15.450
Come on, Momo! Don't mumble 
when you greet someone.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.470
My name is Narumi Tsubame!

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:22.460
We came from Tokyo Game School 
to start our internships today.

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:29.150
This here is Mochizuki Momiji. 
It's nice to meet you.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:33.220
I totally get it. 
Everyone's nervous at first.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:38.970
<i>She never changes...</i>

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.690
Are you two friends?

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.690
Yes. We're the same age 
and grew up together.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.350
I'm studying to become 
a programmer, and Momo...

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:53.460
Mochizuki Momiji wants to work in graphics.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:58.470
Really? Then Mochizuki-san will probably 
be on the character team with me.

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:02.120
<i>She reminds me of Hifumi-senpai.</i>

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.500
Um...

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.750
Y-Yes?

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:08.830
Are school uniforms the company dress code?

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:11.250
No, this is a suit!

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.810
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:14.780
No, it's okay.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:17.610
I've kind of gotten used to wearing this,

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:19.890
but everyone else dresses casually.

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:23.150
Sorry, I'm not used to having 
people newer than me.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:25.550
Mochizuki-san!

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:30.730
May I ask... how old you are?

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:41.260
I'm 19.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:44.090
We're the same age!

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:50.420
Oh, please wait here a moment.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.260
Though it should be safe at this hour.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:56.500
What's this?

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:59.130
Is there something she's 
ashamed to have seen?

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:04.930
<i>A </i>PECO<i> poster? And illustrations 
I haven't seen before.</i>

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:09.250
<i>Plus, a lot of character design sheets...</i>

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:12.320
<i>Could this be Yagami Ko-san's desk?</i>

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:15.570
Sorry! Sometimes she'll be sleeping there,

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:19.730
and I didn't want to ruin 
your first impression of her.

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:22.250
But no worries today.

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:24.530
And who might you be talking about?

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:26.270
Oh, Yagami-san!

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.860
Yagami Ko-san!

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:33.740
You're Mochizuki-san, right? 
And are you the programmer girl?

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:36.970
I'm Narumi Tsubame. 
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:42.390
I-I came here because I want to become a 
character designer like you, Yagami-san!

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:43.970
I'm Mochizuki Momiji!

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:48.750
That's just like me! Let's both do our best!

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.600
Huh? S-Sure...

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.020
Oh, yeah. 
Would you like something to drink?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.710
We have coffee and black tea.

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.860
I'll take some tea!

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:02.120
Same... No sugar, please.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.870
If you want sugar, 
don't feel ashamed to ask.

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:11.250
Like the girl who couldn't drink coffee 
black, but asked for it anyway?

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.450
Not everyone's like you, Aoba.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:17.220
Hey! Please don't say that 
in front of the new people.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:20.760
I'll go pour some tea.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:24.620
Sorry she's so overexcited.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.670
The thought of having people newer 
than her has gone to Aoba's head.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:33.400
It's fine. She seems like a nice person.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:37.510
Well, we've got some time before everyone 
else arrives, so just take it easy.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:41.200
Is this not your desk, Yagami-san?

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.280
That's Aoba's desk.

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:45.720
I-I see.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:49.130
I just saw all the character design sheets...

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:54.670
Yeah. That's because that's Aoba's job.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:00.130
Aoba is <i>PECO</i>'s main character designer.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:03.330
I'm the art director, 
and I do the key visuals.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:08.290
Sorry. I can see how the weird 
advertising tactics might have misled you.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.930
I-It's fine...

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:14.030
<i>So that girl was the 
main character designer?</i>

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:16.660
<i>Didn't she say we were the same age?</i>

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:19.020
<i>I see...</i>

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:22.860
<i>That explains the dumb look that 
I knew wasn't Yagami Ko-san's.</i>

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.700
<i>But I can't deny they're good designs.</i>

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:29.810
<i>Aoba... Aoba...</i>

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:35.080
<i>What was her family name? 
I can never remember.</i>

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:37.750
<i>I think it was Suzu-something...</i>

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:40.550
<i>Oh, yeah!</i>

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.300
<i>Suzumiya Aoba!</i>

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.300
<i>I'll remember it now.</i>

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.050
<i>Uh-oh. Now she's all fired up.</i>

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.140
I'm back!

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:53.430
Um... Huh?

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:58.550
<i>Suzumiya Aoba! Suzumiya Aoba! 
Suzumiya Aoba!</i>

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:03.720
<b>Grrrr...</b>

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:02.990
<i>All of a sudden, 
I'm sensing a very intense gaze.</i>

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.700
Thank you for the tea!

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.660
Oh, sure! This one's yours, Narumi-san.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:11.410
So this one must be Momo's.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:12.980
Here, Momo.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:15.410
Huh? Oh, right...

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:19.370
Man, a character designer 
in your second year? That's amazing!

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:21.850
Not at all! I've still got a ways to go.

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:24.770
When did you start studying art?

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:25.430
So sweet!

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:28.610
Oh, did I mix them up?!

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:31.700
No, I did it to mess with her.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:32.930
Sorry.

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:36.170
<i>Way to ruin my tea </i>and<i> my moment.</i>

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:56.550
Suzumiya-san, I'm not going to lose.

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:01.710
Um... My name is Suzukaze.

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:02.940
Huh?!

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:08.260
<i>Oh, boy. This is gonna get messy.</i>
